<title>SINGAPORE: Jack Chia-MPH says to suspend UK unit.</title>
<headline>Jack Chia-MPH says to suspend UK unit.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1996-09-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Jack Chia-MPH Ltd said on Friday its British subsidiary, Boustead Plc, would be suspended from the London Stock Exchange from September 23 1996.</p>
<p>A company statement said Boustead Plc, which is now a cash company after the sale of its loss-making ACTS Ltd earlier this year, had not been able to acquire a new business to suit the group's core businesses.</p>
<p>The suspension would continue until the group was able to acquire new businesses, it added.</p>
<p>Jack-Chia has interests ranging from publishing to property development.</p>
<p>-- Singapore newsroom (65 8703080)</p>
</text>
